        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-20" edge="1" parent="DPDrP7-kFXSetGJKnKpo-1" source="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-3" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;" target="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-4">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-21" edge="1" parent="DPDrP7-kFXSetGJKnKpo-1" source="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-7" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;" target="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-17">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-22" edge="1" parent="DPDrP7-kFXSetGJKnKpo-1" source="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-8" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;" target="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-9">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-23" edge="1" parent="DPDrP7-kFXSetGJKnKpo-1" source="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-13" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;" target="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-14">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-24" parent="DPDrP7-kFXSetGJKnKpo-1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;size=20;" value="&lt;b&gt;What the reader gets on the SPM tables (record ACLs, DEV)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;dmn_demand: read all (unconditional)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;pm_project: read all&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;pm_program: read all&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;pm_portfolio: read all (OOTB script answers true for users without project_portfolio_user)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;resource_plan: read all&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;cost_plan, cost_plan_breakdown, project_funding: read all (sn_ppm_finance_read)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;sn_align_core_planning_item, sn_gf_goal: no read (needs sn_align_core.ap_read_only / spw_goal_user_read, i.e. the Workspace Viewer group)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;No write, create or delete on any of these tables.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="456" x="24" y="477" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rsvPj1cRMHHYBMWNH137-25" parent="DPDrP7-kFXSetGJKnKpo-1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;darkOpacity=0.05;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;size=20;" value="&lt;b&gt;Gaps to decide (P2, P3)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;P2: custom field ACL cost_plan.* (read, 2019) lists only it_demand_manager, it_demand_user, portfolio_manager, program_manager, project_manager: the reader opens a cost plan and sees empty fields. Add sn_ppm_finance_read.&lt;br&gt;P3: u_cost_distribution read ACL lists only it_project_user (not read-only, contains it_demand_user). Add sn_ppm_finance_read if cost distributions are in scope.&lt;br&gt;Outside SPM records the closure allows: own time cards and time sheets (timecard_user), time card approval (timecard_approver), own PA notes, targets and thresholds (pa_viewer), own planning console configurations (sn_ppm_finance_read), approvals addressed to the user (sn_demand_approver)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="159" width="560" x="512" y="475" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram name="Q1 reader" id="KH-wh7SDHE09Qt90CL21">
    <mxGraphModel dx="2791" dy="965" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="0" tooltips="1" connect="0" arrows="0" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1169" pageHeight="827" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="OYxe-6S0gIPfw5g497Zp-0" />
        <mxCell id="OYxe-6S0gIPfw5g497Zp-1" parent="OYxe-6S0gIPfw5g497Zp-0" />
        <mxCell id="qG1CX550eW5Vu7yh7KZ0-0" parent="OYxe-6S0gIPfw5g497Zp-1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;Q1 - &quot;reading Demand Requester&quot;: read all demands and projects, read-only, no create, no update, without the Demand Manager role. Is there a role or group for that?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Answer:&lt;/b&gt; yes, out of the box and already on the instance. The group &lt;b&gt;Strategic Planning Workspace Viewer&lt;/b&gt; grants exactly this (sn_ppm_read inside sn_align_core.ap_read_only, sn_ppm_finance_read, spw_goal_user_read).&amp;nbsp;&lt;div&gt;No new group, no new role: only the group description in the IAM catalogue and two ACL fixes.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="52" width="1105" x="-1150" y="6" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
